vielotus (2.0.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 2.0.6:
    - Fix Fcitx5 profile management in vielotus-settings --activate:
      keep existing VieLotus entries (e.g. vielotus-vni) in [Groups/0]
      and append the newly activated entry instead of replacing it.
    - Never modify Fcitx5 DefaultIM (including when DefaultIM is already
      vielotus-vni or when initializing a new profile) unless --set-default
      is explicitly passed, and gate fcitx5-remote -s behind --set-default
      so Fcitx5's SetCurrentIM does not overwrite DefaultIM on auto-save/exit.
    - Add regression coverage for the VNI-default + Telex activation
      scenario (including live Fcitx5 daemon exit-save) across Debian Unstable,
      Ubuntu 24.04, and Arch KDE CI gates.

