vielotus (2.0.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 2.0.5:
    - Enforce strict opt-in desktop input-method activation across all Linux
      distributions: installing packages, launching ibus-engine-vielotus,
      opening the vielotus-settings GUI, or toggling engine preferences
      (--telex, --vni, checkboxes) never alters Fcitx5 profile/DefaultIM,
      starts or switches active Fcitx5/IBus engines, edits kwinrc or
      environment.d, or rewrites GNOME Input Sources.
    - Remove ibus-engine-vielotus auto-spawning of vielotus-settings
      (--repair-sources on startup and --telex/--vni on panel menu toggle).
    - Add explicit user confirmation dialog before the GUI doctor "Fix &
      Activate" action modifies desktop input-method lists, and preserve
      existing non-VieLotus Fcitx5 DefaultIM unless --set-default is passed.
    - Remove upstream 51-vielotus-vietnamese.conf, vielotus-onboard.desktop,
      and --auto-onboard across Debian, Ubuntu, Arch, RPM, and generic Linux
      installers (VieLotusIM emits precomposed Unicode NFC; drop obsolete
      debian/patches/ workaround).
  * Regression suite: Native C++20 100.00% (9,091/9,091) primary, 100.00%
    (369/369) ambiguous_both_sides, 100.00% (179/179) whitelist_safe=never;
    Swift 100.00% (9,091/9,091) primary, 98.10% (362/369)
    ambiguous_both_sides, 100.00% (179/179) whitelist_safe=never.

